# interplay_memlive_retarget_discard: Each kind of object is read, the guest points its leaf at a fresh page, and DiscardResources (63) drops what can be dropped: a shared buffer's Metal buffer, a private buffer's, a heap's and a texture's transfer buffer (they turn volatile and stay host-valid), a detach resource's backing. Then a read with flags 0 and one with invalidateHost. In the map setup the flags-0 read makes only the shared buffer again (it has no Metal buffer), over the new page; the others read their host copies (the old bytes) until invalidateHost pages them from the new pages. In the service the shared buffer, the private buffer and the heap are detach resources, attached again at the next exec that lists them whatever its flags: all new at flags 0 but the texture, a host copy, new with invalidateHost. In the blocks setup every read shows the old pages, because the host task still maps them at those VAs; only an UnmapMemory (34) of the four pages and another 63 bring the new pages in, and then every setup reads them.
